Here is another idea along the lines of making polymorphing less of a
give a way. I call it the SCRUBBING BUBBLES approch. There are a
number of monsters that consume items when they pass over them like
rock moles and some types of blobs. Why not generate alot of these
types of monsters on a LEVEL that has alot of objects or in a ROOM
that has alot of polymorphing going on in it.

I think polymorphing is a neat aspect of the game, but it does need
some type of balanceing effect. I have not really liked any of the
other propositions that change the way polymorphing works because they
seem to take the fun out of it. It seems like polymorphing
is abused if one can pile an outrageous number of objects. The
SCRUBBING BUBBLES approch, depending on how it is implemented, could
make it virtually impossible to make a big poly pile. One could assume
that the monsters are attracted to the 'food' items.

If this were implemented properly tools that polymorphed into boxes
could be alowed to have magical items in them again. 

Another suggestion:

The discoveries command '\' should ask [!%*() a]? and there should be
a 'm' option that shows the names of the monsters encountered so far.
Maybe there could be a '*' to show if you have defeated that type of
monster yet.

*r rabid rat 
*r rock mole
 E earth elemental

Another suggestion:

I really wish bags of holding and chests would ask [?!*% a-A] type
questions when putting items into them.
	
